{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1151378-4-5-player-group-looking-for-a-st-for-w-e","id":1151378,"title":"4-5 Player Group looking for a ST for w/e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-20T10:26:51-07:00","id":1151378,"title":"4-5 Player Group looking for a ST for w/e","content":"Was thinking about this for a bit and figured I'd just throw this out there and see if anyone is interested. I'm the guy out of my 4 (occasionally 5) player group that always ends up being the ST/DM 98.7% of the time. They have tried to run games for me in the past but they admit its not their forte or passion. So here goes nothing. Any STs out there looking for a group to run a skype/discord game for? We are used to using roll20 and work really well together. We mostly would be looking to play on the weekends like a Saturday or Sunday schedule, bi weekly is fine but monthly ends up letting interest dwindle. Weekday sessions would work depending on the the time but usually the cut off point is about 10pm on the weekdays so the window is pretty small and not preferred.<br /> <br /> In terms of game preference anything CofD (2nd edition) would probably work. Exalted 3rd would also be great. I think we would be least interested in mortal, vampire, and werewolf just cus we have played those so thoroughly. We are really interested in playing a game together with Scion 2nd Edition when it eventually comes out so we could plan for that as well.<br /> <br /> They are generally used to a mature/gritty style that I usually run but ultimately there is only 3 things we really care about above all. 1. We want a realistic world. 2. We want realistic/consistent consequences for our actions that we need to deal with rather than them being handwaved. 3. We likely will want to go over a few CofD house rules we have in place/like to use for character creation that is universal to every gameline. Also, none of us are afraid or hurt over character death. We play our characters the way they would realistically act and if that ends up getting them into a impossible to avoid death situation then we embrace it and roll a new character with fresh ideas.<br /> <br /> If you are interested in pitching a campaign idea to us feel free to post here or send me a PM. We can talk back and forth here or schedule a time to talk via skype. If we get multiple pitches we will simply talk among each other to figure out which one we would prefer... or hell, maybe play two campaigns. It all depends. The average age of our group is mid 20s to early 30s and we all have plenty of tabletop experience.<br /> <br /> Regardless, tremendous amount of thanks in advance to any interested STs. Trust me, I know how much work goes into running something.<br /> <br /> Timezone: EST","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-20-2017, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}